MyGo v0.9.0: lay out the disk image around a background picture (macos.dmg)

scripts/mygo.mjs applies the patches in file name order, this one after
1-macos-plugins, with `git apply`, before it builds cmd/mygo. Text before
the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

Why: the AstrLink disk image showed its own picture behind the app and the
Applications link, with an arrow and "Drag to Applications to install".
MyGo 0.9 lays out a plain white window and has no option for a
background.

What it changes:
- config: `macos.dmg: { background, width, height, appX, appY,
  applicationsX, applicationsY }`, validated, typed in
  packages/cli/index.d.ts and documented in docs/configuration.md. Without
  it the layout is MyGo's, byte for byte.
- buildDMG copies the picture into the image's hidden .background folder
  and, once the image is mounted, writes the window's .DS_Store again with
  the picture's alias (icvp backgroundImageAlias, backgroundType 2) and
  bookmark (pBBk), which name the file on the mounted volume.
- dmgalias.go encodes both as the mac_alias package (dmgbuild) does for
  Alias.for_file and Bookmark.for_file; the bytes were compared with it on
  a mounted image. dmgalias_darwin.go reads the volume and file attributes
  with getattrlist(2).
- binaryPlist encodes data ([]byte) values.
- tests: the option's validation, the records a background adds, and
  (macOS only) a disk image built with a background.

Upstream status: not submitted. Drop this patch once a MyGo release has an
equivalent option.

